Local fixes for devkitPro/SDL branch switch-sdl-3.4 (c329016c0e338ab4397ad930f83330c9fe058348)
built with devkitA64 r30 (GCC 16.1).

1. SDL_switchkeyboard.c, SDL_switchmouse.c and SDL_switchvideo.c test
   SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_SWITCH before including SDL_internal.h. They only work when
   CMake force-includes SDL_internal.h through its precompiled header. With
   precompiled headers off (needed here: MSYS2 CMake writes a /e/... path into
   cmake_pch.h that the native compiler cannot open; the port also turns PCH off
   for GCC) the whole Switch video driver compiles to nothing, with only a
   -Wundef warning. Include SDL_internal.h first.
2. SDL_switchvideo.c assigned the function SWITCH_IsScreenKeyboardShown to
   device->screen_keyboard_shown, which is a bool in SDL 3.4 (GCC: -Waddress,
   "will always evaluate as true"), so SDL reported the on-screen keyboard as
   always shown. Drop the assignment and report state changes with
   SDL_SendScreenKeyboardShown/Hidden.

Apply with: git -C <SDL clone> apply <this file>

